{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Every ratchet baseline the repo keeps, its stable id (preserved across file moves), and how to measure it, for scripts/gates/check-baseline-growth.mjs (ADR-0250 §11). A measure is a number that may only fall: the check compares it at HEAD against the merge base and fails when it rose, unless the change adds an exception record under scripts/gates/baseline-exceptions/. Measure kinds: `length` (array length or object key count at `path`), `sum` (sum of every numeric leaf under `path`), `value` (the number at `path`), `eachValue` (every numeric leaf under `path`, each compared on its own), `sumLength` (sum of the lengths of every array named `key` under `path`). `path` is dot-separated; an empty path is the document root. A file that holds no ratchet goes under `notRatchets` with the reason, so the coverage test can tell a decision from an omission.",
